WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.954
I’d barely climbed onto the bowsprit when a sail filled up with another breeze and flapped sharply, sounding like a gunshot.

2
00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:12.066
The sail almost hit me, nearly tossing me into the sea.

3
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:16.941
Quickly, I crawled along the bowsprit and tumbled headfirst onto the deck.

4
00:00:16.942 --> 00:00:24.357
From where I landed, I couldn’t see anyone, but the deck, not cleaned since the mutiny, was dirty with footprints.

5
00:00:24.358 --> 00:00:28.140
A broken bottle tumbled to and fro.

6
00:00:28.141 --> 00:00:34.247
Suddenly the Hispaniola went right into the wind, and the whole ship shuddered with a horrible sound.

7
00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:40.947
At the same moment, the mainsail boom groaned and swung aside, and that’s when I saw the two pirates.

8
00:00:40.948 --> 00:00:46.556
Red Cap was stiff and flat on his back with his arms stretched out, like a cross.

9
00:00:46.557 --> 00:00:57.074
Nearby, Israel Hands was leaning against a barrel, his chin on his chest, his hands lying open before him on the deck, and his face deathly white.

10
00:00:57.075 --> 00:01:05.871
The ship kept rising and falling, turning this way and that, as the boom swung to and fro and the mast groaned loudly under the strain.

11
00:01:05.872 --> 00:01:13.531
Blasts of sea spray occasionally drenched the deck, and the men’s bodies swayed with every movement of the ship.

12
00:01:13.532 --> 00:01:17.724
The deck was stained with splashes of dark blood.

13
00:01:17.725 --> 00:01:20.661
"Have they killed each other?" I wondered.

14
00:01:20.662 --> 00:01:24.986
Suddenly Israel Hands turned and moaned with pain.

15
00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:31.689
His jaw was hanging open, and I felt pity for him—until I remembered he had planned to kill us. "Are

16
00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:36.901
you all right, Mr. Hands?" I asked, keeping my distance. "Get

17
00:01:36.902 --> 00:01:42.382
me some brandy," he croaked as he rolled his eyes to try and focus them. "He

18
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:48.206
may be dying," I thought. I raced down the stairs to the captain’s cabin. "What

19
00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:53.140
have they done?" I gasped as I looked at the mess in the cabin. Anything

20
00:01:53.141 --> 00:01:57.838
that had been locked was broken open in the pirates’ search for the map. Mud

21
00:01:57.839 --> 00:02:01.135
covered the floor where they’d sat drinking. The

22
00:02:01.136 --> 00:02:08.471
white walls were smeared with dirty handprints, and dozens of empty bottles clinked together in the corners. The

23
00:02:08.472 --> 00:02:13.879
doctor’s medical book lay open on the table, half of the pages torn out. "They

24
00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:21.308
probably used the pages to light their pipes," I thought in disgust as the lamp still cast its smoky glow. I

25
00:02:21.309 --> 00:02:27.155
went into the galley. The barrels were gone, and empty bottles were lying everywhere. "They

26
00:02:27.156 --> 00:02:31.069
were drunk the whole time!" I said. I

27
00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:37.966
found a bottle with some brandy left, and discovered some biscuits, pickled fruits, cheese, and a bunch of raisins. I

28
00:02:37.967 --> 00:02:42.839
came on deck, went to the water supply , and had a good deep drink. Then

29
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.296
I gave Israel Hands the brandy bottle. The

30
00:02:46.297 --> 00:02:55.833
pirate gulped all he could. "Aye, by thunder," he said, "I needed some brandy!" I

31
00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.773
sat down and ate. "Are

32
00:02:57.774 --> 00:03:00.066
you hurt much?" I asked.

33
00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:07.216
"If that doctor was aboard," growled the pirate, "I’d be all right. But I have no luck."

34
00:03:07.217 --> 00:03:11.792
He pointed to Red Cap. "That swab is good and dead."

35
00:03:11.793 --> 00:03:16.888
Then he looked at me. "And where did you come from?"

36
00:03:16.889 --> 00:03:20.443
"I’m taking possession of this ship, Mr. Hands," I said.

37
00:03:20.444 --> 00:03:24.045
"Please regard me as your captain until further notice."

38
00:03:24.046 --> 00:03:26.946
He looked at me angrily but said nothing.

39
00:03:26.947 --> 00:03:30.138
"I don’t like your flag, Mr. Hands," I told him.

40
00:03:30.139 --> 00:03:35.279
I ran and pulled down their black flag and threw it overboard.

41
00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.217
"God save the king!" I yelled. "Captain Silver has lost!"

42
00:03:40.218 --> 00:03:44.200
The pirate watched me slyly, his chin on his chest.

43
00:03:44.201 --> 00:03:52.717
"I reckon, Captain Hawkins," he said at last, "you’ll want to get ashore now. Let’s talk."

44
00:03:52.718 --> 00:03:57.989
"Why, yes," I replied, "with all my heart, Mr. Hands. Talk on."

45
00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:01.497
I sat down again and continued eating.

46
00:04:01.498 --> 00:04:09.714
"I and this man," he began, nodding at the corpse, "we put the sails up to get her back to the island.

47
00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:17.506
Well, he’s dead now, so who will sail this ship? You can’t; you’re just a boy.

48
00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:29.487
Now, if you give me food and drink and an old handkerchief to tie up my wound , I’ll tell you how to sail her. That’s fair, I think."

49
00:04:29.488 --> 00:04:33.332
"I won’t go back to Captain Kidd’s anchorage," I said.

50
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:36.798
"I’m going to North Inlet and we’ll beach the ship there."

51
00:04:36.799 --> 00:04:42.216
"I know I lost, and you have the better of me," admitted the pirate.

52
00:04:42.217 --> 00:04:50.516
"North Inlet? Fine! I’d help you sail up to Execution Dock if you asked me, by thunder!"

53
00:04:50.517 --> 00:04:55.205
"Good!" I said confidently. "We have a deal then."

54
00:04:55.206 --> 00:05:00.938
In a couple of minutes, I had the Hispaniola sailing easily along the coast of Treasure Island.

55
00:05:00.939 --> 00:05:07.666
"If we sail around the northern point before noon," I thought, "we should reach North Inlet before high tide.

56
00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:11.768
We can beach her safely when the tide permits us to land."

57
00:05:11.769 --> 00:05:17.422
I tied the wheel so the ship wouldn’t go off course and went below to my own sea chest.

58
00:05:17.423 --> 00:05:24.656
I found my mother’s soft silk handkerchief and helped Israel Hands bind up the bleeding stab wound in his thigh.

59
00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:29.896
After he’d eaten a little and drunk more brandy, he sat up and looked like a new man.

60
00:05:29.897 --> 00:05:36.480
The breeze served us well, and we watched the coast of the island passing by swiftly.

61
00:05:36.481 --> 00:05:40.615
"It’s a beautiful day, Mr. Hands," I said cheerfully.

62
00:05:40.616 --> 00:05:46.278
I had plenty of water and good things to eat, and I felt better now about leaving my friends.

63
00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:50.441
My great conquest, in my mind, made up for my desertion.

64
00:05:50.442 --> 00:05:58.436
I would have felt on top of the world except for my companion’s scornful eyes and his odd smile, full of treachery.

65
00:05:58.437 --> 00:06:07.684
Israel Hands craftily watched, and watched, and watched me at my work.

